{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-270090",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,10x+23 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-4x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,20{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}6{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}5x-\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20{x}^{3}-40{x}^{2}+30x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,46{x}^{2}-35x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{46{x}^{2}-92x+69}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,57x-77\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $10x+23,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $57x-77.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{20{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-5x-8}{2{x}^{2}-4x+3}=10x+23+\\frac{57x-77}{2{x}^{2}-4x+3}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
